  "observations": [
    "Whole-matrix NCMTL grouped KS with ER and isolated SI in both matrix baselines.",
    "Fixed five-epoch warm-up produced more stable row assignments and a slightly higher median margin than fixed three-epoch warm-up, but lower validation macro accuracy; stability alone did not predict generalization.",
    "Adaptive all-row sharing was the strongest row method on all three paired validation runs and showed a much narrower across-seed spread than confidence gating.",
    "The 10% gate left 756, 851, and 784 rows independent for seeds 42, 43, and 44. It did not improve validation macro accuracy for any of the three seeds.",
    "Gated seeds 43 and 44 had severe finite-loss spikes at epochs 22 and 23. Their opt checkpoints came from epoch 13, before the spikes; their epoch-30 checkpoints are substantially worse.",
    "A declining gated row-pair match rate does not indicate changing frozen assignments. Shared rows remain close by construction, while independent rows can change their current closest pair.",
    "The contemporary matrix baseline has only seed 42, so a multi-seed claim that adaptive all-row sharing beats matrix-level NCMTL is not supported yet."
  ],
  "recommendation": {
    "among_adaptive_row_methods_for_100_epochs": "all_rows",
    "confidence_gate_0p10": "do_not_use_for_final_run",
    "reason": "All-row adaptive sharing beat 10% gating on validation macro accuracy for every paired seed and avoided the severe late loss spikes seen in two gated runs.",
    "100_epoch_configuration": "Use adaptive row sharing, minimum warm-up 3, maximum warm-up 10, stability threshold 0.90, patience 2, row_min_relative_margin 0.0, no shared activation, auto pooling 0.01, and a new result/checkpoint root. Increase training.num_epochs to 100.",
    "checkpoint_for_reporting": "Select opt using validation macro task accuracy; do not automatically report the epoch-100 checkpoint or select by test accuracy.",
    "monitoring": "Watch validation macro and task accuracies, training/validation loss spikes, and learning-rate reductions; retain the validation-opt checkpoint if later epochs degrade.",
    "limits": [
      "Three paired seeds support a method choice between ungated and 10% gated adaptive row sharing, not a proof of universal superiority.",
      "Gated spike cause is undiagnosed; no NaN was logged and lack of gradient clipping is only a possible contributor, not an established cause.",
      "Seed-42 paired runs used different GPU indices, and the historical matrix run predates the current code revision."
    ]
  }
